Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Mean cosine of the 5,000 shared anchor words to their 1990s vectors, ",
 "before (blue) and after (red) Procrustes alignment. Alignment lifts the \
curve at ",
 "every decade; both necessarily reach 1.0 at the 1990s reference."
}], "Caption",
 CellMargins->{{55, 55}, {2, 
  16}},ExpressionUUID->"f54c649f-a147-4171-a885-aff97ff417b6"],

Cell["\<\
How far from comparable are the raw spaces? The rotation that best aligns the \
1800s onto the 1990s is large: \[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]R \[Minus] I\
\[RightDoubleBracketingBar] = 21.20. For calibration, two unrelated 300-D \
spaces are related by a random rotation with \[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]R \
\[Minus] I\[RightDoubleBracketingBar] \[TildeTilde] 24.50, identical spaces \
give 0, and a perfect mirror-flip gives the maximum 34.60. So the 1800s axes \
begin almost as unrelated to the 1990s as random \[Dash] alignment is \
essential, not cosmetic \[Dash] and the required rotation then shrinks \
smoothly toward the present.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"43db974b-691a-47e9-a2bb-3d2c4a671f99"],

Cell["\<\
Aligning lifts the mean anchor-word cosine to the 1990s at every decade \
(1800s: 0.42 \[Rule] 0.57; 1900s: 0.50 \[Rule] 0.65). That the raw (blue) \
curve already rises, rather than sitting near zero, is itself informative: \
HistWords initialises each decade's training from the previous one, so \
adjacent decades inherit a partial common orientation \[Dash] but that shared \
frame erodes over a century, which is exactly why distant decades must be \
re-aligned.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"cf549906-9dce-474d-87fa-d6951f988b78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Takeaway.  ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Independently trained spaces are not comparable as shipped. One ",
 "orthogonal rotation per decade, fitted on stable high-frequency words, \
makes them ",
 "comparable while leaving each decade's internal geometry untouched."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 12}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.6, 0.4],
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.97, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"0bb79370-351a-4e02-866b-1dc5d2327a2c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. How to read a trajectory", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bf64b2e7-8967-4ae0-be8d-3312ddef7f00"],

Cell["\<\
For one word we collect its aligned vector in every decade it occurs, gather \
the nearest neighbours that anchor each era of its meaning, and project that \
whole local neighbourhood to two dimensions with PCA. The word's path then \
threads between an early-meaning cluster and a late-meaning cluster; colour \
runs from blue (1800s) to red (1990s).\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"4bbef372-963a-46e8-9209-e04e0ac21d50"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["What the projection does and does not say.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " The 2-D layout is a ",
 StyleBox["per-word",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " PCA of that word's own cloud, chosen to spread its motion across ",
 "the page; absolute positions and the axes themselves carry no global \
meaning, and ",
 "2-D distances are an approximation of the true 300-D ones. The trustworthy \
signal is ",
 StyleBox["which neighbours sit at each end",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " of the path and ",
 "how far the word ",
 "travels between them",
 " \[Dash] both of which come straight from the high-"
}], "dimensional cosine geometry, not the projection.", \
"Text",ExpressionUUID->"ec2c5aa3-1dd1-46f3-a185-43dad537de72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 CellMargins -> {{50, 50}, {6, 6}}], "Input",
 CellLabel->" In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b3d830be-1f78-47b9-8f9a-610ca9edcebb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": the path lingers among ",
 "merry, cheerful, ",
 "joyous, lively, gaiety",
 " through the blue and purple decades, then swings sharply ",
 "red-ward to ",
 StyleBox["homosexual, lesbian, gays, bisexual",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " by the 1990s \[Dash] a "
}], "two-century meaning change rendered as a single sweep across the page.", \
"Caption",ExpressionUUID->"bfff18da-5390-43d7-be4c-a7d2acd254d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 CellMargins -> {{55, 55}, {2, 16}}], "Input",
 CellLabel->" In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5ca367ff-8617-434f-81aa-02f5119982a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Takeaway.  ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Read a trajectory by its ",
 StyleBox["endpoints and their neighbours",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", not by the exact shape of the curve. The neighbours are the evidence; the \
curve is ",
 "just their geometry."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 12}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.6, 0.4],
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.97, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"a7a4c5b6-86b9-4cf7-b699-b61669984cde"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Explore all fourteen words", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"05d73f6f-a6be-4bac-9fa8-41268c6311fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Rather than print fourteen separate plots, the construction above is wired ",
 "into one interactive ",
 StyleBox["Manipulate",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". Pick a word, scrub the time slider to ",
 "reveal the path decade by decade, and toggle the neighbour labels. The \
static image ",
 "below shows one state (",
 StyleBox["gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", full path); evaluate the code cell beneath ",
 "it in the live notebook for the interactive version."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"203d39d4-3818-4547-abe9-4778fcfc0170"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A few worth visiting: ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (agricultural ",
 "sow / ",
 "seed / scatter",
 " \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["radio / television / bbc",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "); ",
 StyleBox["computer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (a V from human surnames through ",
 StyleBox["electronic / circuits",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["software / internet",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "); ",
 StyleBox["mouse",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (keeps ",
 StyleBox["rat / cat",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " but grows a second ",
 StyleBox["cursor / click / keyboard",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " cluster); ",
 StyleBox["web",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (spider \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["www / browser / server",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "); ",
 StyleBox["terrific",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["awful",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (the two halves of a terror-to-praise swap); and ",
 StyleBox["guy",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (the Guy Fawkes effigy \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["fellow / chap / dude",
  FontSlant->Italic]
}], ").", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"594e2ff5-6131-434f-ab8a-9845330fcc5e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 CellMargins -> {{50, 50}, {6, 6}}], "Input",
 CellLabel->" In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"617d0e17-7268-4771-9a3d-3042d17f6e05"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "The \[Section]5 explorer. In the live notebook the cell below is an ",
 "interactive ",
 StyleBox["Manipulate",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (choose a word, scrub the decade slider, toggle ",
 "neighbour labels); the PDF / web view shows its default state (",
 StyleBox["gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", full path)."
}], "Caption",
 CellMargins->{{55, 55}, {2, 
  16}},ExpressionUUID->"bfc59270-0a45-4f4e-98e3-39955b2c2365"],

